(The single basic block ends with the call and is followed immediately by the closing `}` — no `exit;`, no `trap;`, no `ret;`. The unreachable block has no CFG terminator. Identical broken output is produced with the additional flag -no-trap-after-noreturn, which is the configuration that actually routes through the buggy isLoweredToTrap() Naked omission. In a multi-block divergent function the %unlikely block is likewise left unterminated as `call.uni sideeffect, ();` immediately before the function's closing brace.)

expected:
The pass should insert the `exit;` inline asm before the unreachable so the block has a terminator, matching the behavior for the same naked function WITHOUT -trap-unreachable (which correctly emits):

	call.uni sideeffect, ();
	} // callseq 0
	// begin inline asm
	exit;
	// end inline asm

i.e. since SelectionDAG (via UnreachableInst::shouldLowerToTrap) emits NO trap for a naked function, NVPTXLowerUnreachable must insert `exit;` to terminate the block and prevent ptxas (PTXVersion<8.3) from inferring a spurious fall-through CFG edge that widens divergent regions. Fix: add the missing `if (getFunction()->hasFnAttribute(Attribute::Naked)) return false;` to isLoweredToTrap() so it stays in sync with shouldLowerToTrap (and note the runOnFunction early-out at lines 136-137 also masks the bug unless -no-trap-after-noreturn is set).

